####################################################################
# reduced_pulmonary_function.dlog — HAND-AUTHORED. NOT GENERATED.
#
# TRIED as an on-demand query and REVERTED — kept as a STANDING rule. See
# cardiac_arrest.dlog's own header for the full reasoning (identical
# rationale: unscoped, unconditional-per-alarm check, worse on demand).
#
# One rule per file (split out of the former clinical_rules.dlog) so
# poc_entry.py can enable/disable each rule independently. RDFox Datalog
# port of FRAMEWORK/KNOWLEDGE_BASE/clinicalEvents.ttl's
# ReducedPulmonaryFunctionCondition — see cardiac_arrest.dlog's header
# (same design) and the migration plan for full background.
#
# metric:RespirationVolume_Minute specifically, not the broader
# metric:RespirationVolume — same over-match reasoning as the OWL
# original (a low TIDAL volume alone does not carry the same clinical
# weight).
####################################################################

@prefix mda:          <https://w3id.org/mda/ontology#> .
@prefix metric:       <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/metric/> .
@prefix metricRate:   <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/metric-rate/> .
@prefix clinicalEvent: <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/clinical-event/> .

[?process, mda:impliesClinicalEvent, clinicalEvent:ReducedPulmonaryFunction] ?gRate :-
    [?metric, rdf:type, metric:RespirationVolume_Minute] ?gType,
    [?metric, mda:hasRate, metricRate:Decreased] ?gRate,
    [?metric, mda:approximates, ?property] ?gApprox,
    [?property, mda:isPropertyOf, ?process] .

# VALIDATION — executed against real RDFox: positive
# (RespirationVolume_Minute + hasRate Decreased) → 1. the exact over-match
# risk (RespirationVolume_Tidal + hasRate Decreased) → 0, confirming the
# Minute-specific anchoring genuinely excludes it under RDFox's own join
# semantics, not just in the axiom's prose.
